.TH ZERODDS-OPCUA-BRIDGED 1 "" "ZeroDDS" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-opcua-bridged \- the OMG DDS-OPCUA Gateway 1.0 daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zerodds-opcua-bridged
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-bind\fR \fIADDR\fR]
[\fB\-\-domain\fR \fIID\fR]
[\fB\-\-idl\fR \fIFILE\fR]...
[\fB\-\-gateway\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-V\fR | \fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zerodds-opcua-bridged
implements the OMG DDS-OPCUA Gateway 1.0 (formal/2020-01-01) as a running
process: an
.I opc.tcp
server exposing DDS topics in its AddressSpace (Gateway 1.0 \(sc9,
including Historical Access, \(sc9.3.4), an OPC-UA client
browsing/subscribing configured foreign servers into DDS (\(sc8), and OPC
Foundation Part 14 (UADP) PubSub over UDP multicast, both directions,
optionally secured (Part 14 \(sc8, build feature
.BR pubsub-security ).
Per-session
.B acl.rules
enforcement backs a
.I Write
against this server's own AddressSpace; OTLP lifecycle spans are exported
when
.B metrics.otlp_endpoint
is set.
.PP
DDS types are resolved from an operator-supplied
.I .idl
file, never a compiled Rust type, through the reflective
.I SerializedTypeSupport
layer.
.PP
Implements
.IR docs/specs/zerodds-opcua-bridge-1.0.md .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-config =\fIFILE\fR
Path to the config file (YAML). See
.BR zerodds-opcua-bridged.yaml (5).
.TP
.BR \-\-bind =\fIADDR\fR
.I opc.tcp
bind address. Default:
.IR 0.0.0.0:4840 .
.TP
.BR \-\-domain =\fIID\fR
DDS domain ID. Default: 0.
.TP
.BR \-\-idl =\fIFILE\fR
IDL file to compile (repeatable); the types
.B opcua.gateway_config
and
.B opcua.client.servers[].nodes[]
name must be declared in one of these files.
.TP
.BR \-\-gateway\-config =\fIFILE\fR
Path to the Spec \(sc10 XML gateway configuration (bridge/connection defs).
.TP
.BR \-\-log\-level =\fILEVEL\fR
One of
.IR trace ", " debug ", " info ", " warn ", " error .
.TP
.BR \-\-metrics =\fIADDR\fR
Prometheus listener.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Version info.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the option synopsis.
.TP
.BR \-\-set " \fIPATH\fR=\fIVALUE\fR"
One setting above every file, repeatable;
.BI + PATH = VALUE
appends to a list.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-config
Validate and print the effective configuration with the origin of every
value, then exit: 0 valid, 1 invalid value or unknown key, 2 unreadable
file, syntax error or include cycle.
.SH SIGNALS
SIGTERM/SIGINT stop the daemon: the
.I opc.tcp
accept loop and the metrics listener both wake, every worker thread is
joined, then the process exits 0.
.br
SIGHUP re-reads
.B acl.default_deny
/
.B acl.rules
from the same sources the process started with; a file that fails to load
changes nothing. Changing
.BR domain ", " opcua.server.bind ,
the IDL/gateway-config-driven topic set (including any
.IR node_id / browse_path
override and
.BR opcua.server.historical.topics ),
.BR acl.users ", " acl.allow_anonymous ,
.B opcua.pubsub.connections[].security
or
.B metrics.otlp_endpoint
needs a restart \(em SIGHUP's scope has not widened past
.BR acl.default_deny / acl.rules .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NOTIFY_SOCKET
systemd
.B Type=notify
readiness/stop notification, sent automatically when set.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal shutdown.
.TP
.B 1
Configuration error.
.TP
.B 2
.I opc.tcp
bind error \(em address in use.
.TP
.B 3
DDS init error.
.TP
.B 4
SecureChannel/certificate setup error.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/zerodds/opcua-bridged.yaml .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-opcua-bridged.yaml (5).
OMG DDS-OPCUA Gateway 1.0 (formal/2020-01-01); OPC Foundation Part 4, Part 6,
Part 14.
